    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the median, $Q_1$, $Q_3$ and the interquartile range.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Median $=38.5$ ms, $Q_1=32.5$ ms, $Q_3=44$ ms, IQR $=11.5$ ms.",
          "worked": "In ascending order:\n\n$22,25,30,31,31,34,35,35,36,38,39,40,42,43,44,44,45,46,48,62$.\n\nThere are 20 values. Average the 10th and 11th values for the median. Each half contains 10 values; average the middle two values of each half for its quartile.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Median}&=\\frac{38+39}{2}\\\\\\text{Median}&=38.5\\text{ ms}\\\\Q_1&=\\frac{31+34}{2}\\\\Q_1&=32.5\\text{ ms}\\\\Q_3&=\\frac{44+44}{2}\\\\Q_3&=44\\text{ ms}\\\\\\text{IQR}&=44-32.5\\\\\\text{IQR}&=11.5\\text{ ms}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Construct a boxplot.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Box from $32.5$ to $44$ ms, median at $38.5$ ms, whiskers at $22$ and $48$ ms; mark $62$ ms separately as an outlier.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Lower fence}&=32.5-1.5\\times11.5\\\\\\text{Lower fence}&=15.25\\text{ ms}\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=44+1.5\\times11.5\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=61.25\\text{ ms}\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe lowest and highest data values within the fences are $22$ and $48$ ms. Draw the box from $32.5$ to $44$ ms with its median at $38.5$ ms. Extend the whiskers to $22$ and $48$ ms and show $62$ ms with a separate marker.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p15-q7-b-boxplot",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=2.4mm,y=1mm,draw=black,text=black,line width=0.5pt]\n\\draw (18,0)--(65,0);\n\\foreach \\x in {20,30,40,50,60}{\\draw (\\x,0)--(\\x,2);\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{8.5}{10}\\selectfont] at (\\x,0){\\x};}\n\\draw (22,10)--(32.5,10);\n\\draw (32.5,6) rectangle (44,14);\n\\draw (38.5,6)--(38.5,14);\n\\draw (44,10)--(48,10);\n\\fill (62,11.3)--(61.3,8.7)--(62.7,8.7)--cycle;\n\\node[below,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont] at (41.5,-7){Reaction time (ms)};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 120,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 15,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 7(b); teacher PDF page 83, Exercise 18C 7(b)",
                "description": "Self-contained horizontal boxplot with a triangular marker at 62; whiskers end at the extreme non-outlier observations.",
                "mathematics": "Q1=32.5, median=38.5, Q3=44; whiskers 22 and 48; outlier 62. Axis ticks 20,30,40,50,60.",
                "answerVisibility": "solution only"
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Identify any outliers.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$62$ ms is the only outlier.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Lower fence}&=32.5-1.5\\times11.5\\\\\\text{Lower fence}&=15.25\\text{ ms}\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=44+1.5\\times11.5\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=61.25\\text{ ms}\\end{align*}$$\n\nOnly $62$ ms lies outside these fences, since $62>61.25$. It is the only outlier.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
